DSH Nexus

A unified integration for DeepSeek Harness Desktop 0.2.1-rc.2.
The Nexus composition, adapters and user interface combine components with
different license conditions; consult LICENSE and THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md.

Product attribution:
  billion-context / acp-kernel
  https://github.com/ranxianglei/billion-context
  The original license and additional product-surface attribution terms
  are retained in vendor/acp-kernel/LICENSE and the source notices.

Selected source families include dsh-memory and memory-evolve, dsh-mnemon,
memsearch, turn-rewind, Agency Agents, dsh-web and its 19 subpackages,
ThoughtDAG, Synapse, Archify, Aegis, Superpowers, J-Space, the qiudeng
engineering methods, and Metis. The complete 36-unit source identities,
selected paths, revisions, notices and outstanding runtime validation
are listed in sources.lock.json and the delivery coverage report.

Metis notices retain both Wholiver and Mario Zechner copyrights.
ThoughtDAG and Synapse notices are retained under assets/notices/.
ws and the xterm terminal packages retain their MIT notices under
assets/notices/runtime-dependencies/. qrcode.react 4.2.0 is ISC,
Copyright (c) 2015 Paul O’Shannessy. Its bundled QR Code Generator is MIT,
Copyright (c) Project Nayuki. Both complete license texts are retained.
Restricted code-review source is not copied; Nexus implements that
capability separately. Remote services, optional external executables
and third-party marketplace resources are not relicensed by Nexus.

DSH-agent-procedures and Nexus-Aethra/Nexus-Terminal 0.1.14 retain their
original MIT licenses and archive identities under vendor/agent-procedures/
and vendor/nexus-terminal/. Their original tools, native dshell interface
and registration model are preserved with a separate Windows/DSH adapter.

No user account credentials, private sessions, machine profiles or
deployment recovery snapshots are part of this distribution.
